WEBVTT

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:08.156
One line on this plan reads 12,170.

00:00:08.456 --> 00:00:10.571
It's the diagonal, not the wall.

00:00:11.021 --> 00:00:15.605
Misread it, and that plot's £157 short.

00:00:16.705 --> 00:00:19.000
So we built Drawing-to-Quote Engine.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.946
Drop in the whole pack. It finds the three pages that matter,

00:00:24.146 --> 00:00:28.466
and proposes every measurement, right beside the line it came from.

00:00:28.866 --> 00:00:35.443
So when it reads 12.17, the estimator sees the diagonal, and puts 13.

00:00:35.943 --> 00:00:41.005
Everything follows. The perimeter. The lifts. The price.

00:00:41.605 --> 00:00:47.913
If the drawing doesn't say, it leaves the field empty, and won't price until someone fills it.

00:00:48.413 --> 00:00:51.380
The rate band stays the estimator's call.

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:57.062
Then every line goes into the estimating system, with the page it came from.

00:00:58.562 --> 00:01:06.111
Across a forty-plot phase, that's £6,294 that no longer gets given away.

00:01:08.911 --> 00:01:11.972
The drawings arrive. The quote follows.
